<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/triple-decker.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/triple-decker-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/triple-decker.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="/rhode-island-communities/">Communities</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span>Cranston</nav><p class="tag">Providence metro</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Cranston, Rhode Island</h1><p class="lede">Cranston runs from dense neighborhoods near Providence to farms and woods in the west, so a claim can mean a triple-decker or a rural colonial with a well.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn sun" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn glass" href="/request-a-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Providence County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Providence metro</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="note"><p class="note-t">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips"><li>River flooding history</li><li>Tree fall</li><li>Nor’easter wind</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Fire</li></ul></div>
<p>Insurance appraisal in Cranston reflects a city with two personalities. Near Providence, closely spaced houses mean wind, fire and water damage can affect more than one building. In western Cranston, mature trees and long driveways make storm cleanup and access part of the loss.</p>
<h2>Claims we see in Cranston</h2>
<ul>
<li>Tree impacts on roofs and porches after nor’easters and tropical storms</li>
<li>Wind damage to roofs and vinyl siding, with matching questions on the undamaged sides</li>
<li>Interior water losses from burst pipes and ice dams</li>
<li>Fire and smoke damage in multi-family homes</li>
</ul>
<h2>Edgewood and Pawtuxet homes</h2>
<p>Many Edgewood houses have original details, from leaded windows to hardwood floors laid in patterns. Replacing those properly costs more than a generic line item, and we price them accordingly.</p><h2>Neighborhoods and villages we cover in Cranston</h2><ul class="chips plain"><li>Edgewood</li><li>Pawtuxet</li><li>Garden City</li><li>Knightsville</li><li>Eden Park</li><li>Auburn</li><li>Western Cranston</li></ul><h2>Housing in Cranston</h2><p>Eastern Cranston has early twentieth-century homes and multi-family houses in Edgewood and near Pawtuxet Village. Garden City and Knightsville have postwar neighborhoods. Western Cranston is more rural, with larger lots, newer colonials and older farmhouses.</p><h2>Cranston storm history</h2><ul class="mini-timeline"><li><b>2010</b><span>The Pawtuxet River crested at a record level at the Cranston gauge during the March floods.</span></li><li><b>2011</b><span>Tropical Storm Irene brought down trees across the city.</span></li><li><b>2015</b><span>The January blizzard dropped heavy snow on roofs.</span></li><li><b>2017</b><span>An October nor’easter caused widespread tree and power-line damage.</span></li></ul><h2>Services available in Cranston</h2><p>Every Rhode Island Insurance Appraiser service is available to owners in Cranston and nearby towns, including:</p><ul><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/appraisal-clause-advocacy/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/homeowner-claim-valuation/">Homeowner Claim Valuation</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/commercial-condo-hoa-claims/">Commercial, Condo &amp; HOA Claims</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/roof-hail-claim-valuation/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/wind-microburst-tornado-claims/">Wind, Microburst &amp; Tornado Damage</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/hurricane-tropical-storm-claims/">Hurricane &amp; Tropical Storm Claims</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/water-leak-sewer-backup-claims/">Water Damage &amp; Leak Claims</a></li></ul><h2>Questions from Cranston owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you inspect in western Cranston?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, including rural properties with outbuildings, which may fall under other structures coverage.</p></div></details><details><summary>A neighbor’s tree hit my house. Whose policy pays?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually your own policy covers damage to your house, whoever owned the tree. Your insurer may pursue the neighbor if negligence is involved.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you match old hardwood flooring?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>We price the work needed to achieve a reasonable match, which can include more area than the damaged boards alone.</p></div></details></div><h2>Nearby communities</h2><div class="related"><a href="/rhode-island-communities/providence/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Providence</span><svg class="ic" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/rhode-island-communities/warwick/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Warwick</span><svg c